      "title": "Generally Available: Azure Ephemeral OS Disk with full caching for VM/VMSS ",
      "description": "<div style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\" lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin: 0px; user-select: text; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 19.425px; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-variant-ligatures: none !important; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><span style=\"margin: 0px; user-select: text; box-shadow: rgb(15, 108, 189) 2px 0px 0px 0px;\">Azure Ephemeral OS Disk with full caching is now generally available for new virtual machines and Virtual Machine Scale Sets. The capability caches the complete OS image on a VM’s local storage, eliminating remote-storage reads after caching finishes. This delivers consistently fast, low-millisecond OS disk access, up to 10× better I/O performance, and greater resilience during storage interruptions—without slowing VM provisioning because caching runs asynchronously after boot. It is designed for I/O-sensitive, stateless workloads such as AI training and inference, quorum-based databases, real-time analytics, and large-scale services. Full caching uses a VM’s cache, resource, or NVMe disk and reduces available local capacity by twice the OS disk size.</span></span></div><div style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-variant-ligatures: none; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-variant-ligatures: none; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-variant-ligatures: none; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">It is available across Azure public regions for supported 8-core-and-larger GPU, storage-optimized, memory-optimized, HPC, general-purpose, and compute-optimized VM series. Customers can enable it through Azure CLI, ARM templates, or REST APIs by setting the full-caching option for Ephemeral OS disks.</span></div>",
